WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
- The auditions were, obviously,

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.700
a very important part of the show.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.880
Do you have any that stick out?

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.900
I do, but you go first.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.000
Do you have any auditions that stick out

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.040
that were just funny?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.110
- Where do we begin?

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:09.970
- It was the great ones
and the funny ones.

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.890
What was the guy that was the lion?

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.770
He thought he was a lion or something.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.090
- But that was real, reality.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.760
Because no one had seen the show before.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.020
So, we saw and heard some of
the worst singers in America.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.760
They just kept throwing
them onto the show.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.388
So, we're sitting there going,

00:00:25.388 --> 00:00:28.047
"What the hell is going on?"

00:00:28.958 --> 00:00:30.700
- What are we doing here?
- Suppose to be a talent show.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:31.533
- I will say this.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.910
I went right after the girl
that sang Lady Marmalade

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.210
in, like, opera form.

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:37.343
Like, she was like,

00:00:37.343 --> 00:00:38.307
♪ Gitchie, gitchie, ya-ya ♪

00:00:38.307 --> 00:00:41.501
And I literally was like,
"Oh, I think I have this."

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.319
(laughing)

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:44.152
I was like...

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:45.471
I was like, okay.

00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:47.580
Okay, if they didn't like that,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.810
they might like what I'm doing.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.120
I was like, "What the hell just happened?"

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.010
- That was good timing.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:53.190
Well I think that's what we said

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.450
at the end of the audition shows.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:55.970
What the hell just happened?

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.230
I swear to God, Kelly.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:00.230
I thought this is gonna
be such a disaster.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.890
I didn't even know, I
went back to England.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.220
I didn't even know the show was on.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:06.190
And I got this phone
call from this producer

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.727
who was screaming down the
phone saying, you know,

00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:08.650
"You gotta hit."

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.637
And I said, "What?"

00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:10.990
"The show aired last night."

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:11.947
I went, "Really?"

00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:13.350
"And it's a hit."

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.670
I went, "What?"

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.020
I really thought it would
last about two weeks

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.853
and we'd get--
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:01:17.853 --> 00:01:18.710
- Yeah, I thought we'd
get thrown off the air.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.002
- Yeah, all of us.

00:01:20.002 --> 00:01:21.000
None of us knew.
- But we had the best,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.508
fun time on the road.
- [Paula] I knew, I knew.

00:01:22.508 --> 00:01:24.563
- [Randy] You knew it was gonna work?

00:01:24.563 --> 00:01:26.162
- It was such a cool show.

00:01:26.162 --> 00:01:28.440
Do you have any criticism that you regret?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.127
Or just things that
happened and you're like,

00:01:30.127 --> 00:01:31.680
"Maybe I didn't hear it right, or?"

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.110
- I wish we never used the word "blamang".

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.980
That was his idea with these crazy words.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.360
- We use to give each other
a word you had to say.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.720
- No, it was called the name game.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.060
And it was during a live show.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.000
And Simon would, it's like
he was so excited about it.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.530
And I will say, it was damn funny.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:47.363
- Wait, what's the name game?

00:01:47.363 --> 00:01:48.935
- The name game, he did this.

00:01:48.935 --> 00:01:49.768
- We would write down a piece of paper.

00:01:49.768 --> 00:01:50.601
I say, "Whatever happens,

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.787
"you have to use this word in critique."

00:01:52.787 --> 00:01:53.881
- But he did this.

00:01:53.881 --> 00:01:55.281
- [Kelly] You have to work it in?

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.114
- During a live show.

00:01:56.114 --> 00:02:00.317
And he said, he goes, "Randy,
Paula, here's my black card.

00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:03.067
"Ten minutes on Rodeo
Drive if you incorporate

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:04.571
"these words into your critique."

00:02:04.571 --> 00:02:06.083
- Yeah, blamang.
- No, Randy yours was--

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.760
- Blamang is an English dessert.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:10.120
- No, you gave Randy spotted dick.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:14.275
Which is a British dessert.
- Oh yeah, oh yeah, oh yeah.

00:02:14.275 --> 00:02:15.934
- How did you work that in?

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:19.545
- Yes, he did.
- Simon, hang on, hang on...

00:02:19.545 --> 00:02:21.259
- Did you fit that in?

00:02:21.259 --> 00:02:22.940
- No he didn't.
- Yeah, he did.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.767
- No, he wouldn't do
it and you said to me,

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.892
"Double down, I'll give you 15
minutes with my credit card."

00:02:28.892 --> 00:02:29.842
- Wait a minute.

00:02:29.842 --> 00:02:30.750
Explain to Kelly what that is.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.960
- Well, it is an old
fashioned English dessert.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.220
If you go on Google...

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.580
- Please google "spotted dick"
- Spotted dick.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.576
- Then delete your Google search history.

00:02:40.576 --> 00:02:41.409
- It's a dessert.

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:44.620
- But it will tell you, it's a pudding.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.537
And then when we did the live shows,

00:02:45.537 --> 00:02:48.147
and we were under pressure,
Paula would suddenly say to me,

00:02:48.147 --> 00:02:50.870
"Uh, give me something to say,
you know, when people leave."

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.540
So, I would make up these,
like, Chinese proverbs,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.387
which are nonsensical, by the way.

00:02:56.387 --> 00:02:59.200
- So this is a show within
a show that we all missed?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.294
- None of you knew.
- Yes, we had a blast.

00:03:01.294 --> 00:03:03.127
- The moth that eats the melon
- Simon, yes, he'd say--

00:03:03.127 --> 00:03:04.396
- You had the moth that eats the melon.

00:03:04.396 --> 00:03:05.557
- He goes, "Paula, you're so boring.

00:03:05.557 --> 00:03:07.327
"You just have nothing to say
interesting, you're so boring.

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:08.877
"Say, 'The moth that finds a melon ball

00:03:08.877 --> 00:03:10.256
"inside of a won ton.'"

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.206
- Listen.

00:03:11.206 --> 00:03:12.083
- What a bully!

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:13.170
- That lasted--

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:15.397
- I was trying to help her.
- And all I hear is that.

00:03:15.397 --> 00:03:17.060
And then Ryan goes, "Paula?"

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.597
And I'm crying laughing and
I go, "He said the moth that

00:03:20.597 --> 00:03:22.140
"finds a melon ball."

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.760
- And then you look crazy!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.593
- Yeah, and then--

00:03:24.593 --> 00:03:25.649
- And we would go, like, "What?"

00:03:25.649 --> 00:03:27.304
- Simon goes like this to the camera.

00:03:27.304 --> 00:03:28.530
(audience laughs)

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.050
- Oh my God, you teed her up.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.517
- Yeah, we have to have fun.

00:03:31.517 --> 00:03:33.677
We were having fun.
- At my expense.

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:34.920
- I actually love this though
because you had fun doing it.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.380
Would y'all ever work together again?

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.765
- 100%
- Of course, yes.

00:03:37.765 --> 00:03:40.456
- Oh my gosh, let's do this.

00:03:40.456 --> 00:03:42.437
Oh my gosh.
(audience cheers)

00:03:42.437 --> 00:03:45.704
All right, well American Idol
launched huge superstars.

00:03:45.704 --> 00:03:48.470
Oscar winner, Jennifer Hudson.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.420
Eight times platinum, Carrie Underwood.

00:03:52.308 --> 00:03:55.300
Queen's lead singer, I have
heard this dude in person,

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:56.410
he is so good.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.185
Adam Lambert is amazing.

00:03:58.185 --> 00:03:59.505
- So good.
- He's a great guy, as well.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.230
- So, who blew you away from day one?

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.063
I was sneaky.

00:04:03.063 --> 00:04:03.920
I know everybody everybody didn't kind of

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.753
remember me for a minute.

00:04:04.753 --> 00:04:06.120
Like, who blew you away from day one?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.720
'Cause for me, I was
blown away with, honestly,

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.000
Tamyra and Justin on my season.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.264
- Tamyra and Justin.
- Tamyra and Justin,

00:04:11.264 --> 00:04:15.350
but then you came in and
you were so raw and honest

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.697
with no pretense that I was like,

00:04:16.697 --> 00:04:18.220
"Yo, she's fire right there."

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.040
- I remember thinking,
"What just happened?"

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:22.873
- [Kelly] Really?
- Oh yeah.

00:04:22.873 --> 00:04:23.900
- [Paula] You were so clever.
- Even if you're lying,

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.137
I'll take it.

00:04:25.137 --> 00:04:26.580
- [Paula] No, no.
- [Simon] No, I swear to God.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.250
- You knew who you were as an artist,

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.640
you picked the right songs,
and I'll never forget

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.751
the biggest treat, is I
was riding in the elevator

00:04:32.751 --> 00:04:36.140
at CBS with you, and you were vocalizing,

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.960
and you were singing opera.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.910
And I was like, "Is there
anything this girl can't do?"

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.781
- And you were such a natural.

00:04:42.781 --> 00:04:44.840
You were just like, you had
that whole soulful vibe.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.020
You were just natural with it.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:46.853
- Well, thank...

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.830
I actually agree with that,
with like, the whole season.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.940
Our first season, it was so new.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.710
None of us knew, we weren't entitled,

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.250
'cause everybody was just trying
to pay their electric bill,

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.251
people, like nobody...

00:04:55.251 --> 00:04:58.110
We didn't think it was
gonna go anywhere, and so,

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.210
you know, we were kids at camp.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.430
And it was something so cool
about that first season.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.400
I will so though
- [Simon] Underrated.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.280
- After working that
season, I will never do

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.113
something as hard.

00:05:05.113 --> 00:05:06.450
They worked us so hard.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.940
Like, we were doing so many
things and everybody, like,

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.410
they're like, "Oh your
schedule's so busy now."

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.200
And I'm like, "Whatever."
- And the movie,

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.068
I've gotta tell you,
that's a standing ovation.

00:05:15.068 --> 00:05:15.901
- [Randy] Yes.

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:18.959
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

00:05:18.959 --> 00:05:21.199
- How that never got an Oscar...

00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:22.258
- I don't know.

00:05:22.258 --> 00:05:24.138
- Kelly, you gotta know something.

00:05:24.138 --> 00:05:24.977
- Remake.
- He knows.

00:05:24.977 --> 00:05:27.850
He is totally messing
with me, 'cause he knows

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.417
how much I hate that film.

00:05:29.417 --> 00:05:30.347
- I would do a remake.

00:05:30.347 --> 00:05:32.620
- I can't stand you
- Simon wants you to be in it.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.840
- I'll do it, if you'll be in it.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.417
- Okay, deal.
- Okay.

00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:36.359
- Okay, shoot.

00:05:36.359 --> 00:05:38.609
- Mine's a very small part.

00:05:38.609 --> 00:05:39.929
- [Kelly] Whatever.
- Oh my God.

00:05:39.929 --> 00:05:41.150
- But every single one
of you saw it, right?

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.668
- No you didn't.
(audience cheers)

00:05:42.668 --> 00:05:43.740
Liars!

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.720
- Oh, if you haven't, please,
please, please treat yourself.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.070
- I literally told my
nanny she would be fired

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.503
if she showed my children.

